CORE
main.cpp

^\[difference\.pointer_arithmetic\.\d+\] .*: SUCCESS$
^\[less\.pointer_arithmetic\.\d+\] .*: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ null minus null: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ null less than null: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^\[(difference|less)\.pointer_arithmetic\.\d+\] .*: FAILURE$
--
The pointer checks of a subtraction or relation accept two null pointers in
C++ only; in C (C11 6.5.6/9, 6.5.8/5) they still fail
(regression/cbmc/ptr_arithmetic_on_null).
